Did the exact same thing; Summer was the only citizen out, and would have been the 5th in Dawn&#39;s trash if I let Hayes kill her. &nbsp;Hated to see Decoy Projection go, but not flipping Dawn was more important.

&nbsp;

 Near Mint, although I&#39;ll admit after seeing that the game started with empty hands for the heroes, I came here to read first. &nbsp; When I saw the order of the day was &quot;Hit Dawn with everything you&#39;ve got, and only worry about Citizens/Environments that are really killing you,&quot; the rest became academic. &nbsp;By Round 3-4, I had the Staff, Imbued Fire, and the Explosives Wagon out, so every hero was hitting Dawn for at least +2 DMG/hit; Ra (Staff) and Expatriette (Nemesis) were doing +3. &nbsp;Finished her off in Round 7 with a DW Fixer Overdrive (5 pts each hit), but had 23 more points of pain in store for Dawn on the upcoming turns of Ra (Flame Strike (5 pts) + Living Conflag (4 pts) + Base Power (5 pts)), and DW Expatriette (RPG (4 pts) + Pride (5 pts)). &nbsp;Could also have destroyed the Explosives Wagon on DW Expat&#39;s last turn for 4 more points, if necessary. &nbsp;
